+      "content": "With the subjunctive, *mientras* can measure time (*mientras dure la lluvia*: for as long as the rain lasts) or set a condition (*mientras no hagas ruido*). The second use means the same as *siempre que* \"provided that\". You know *siempre que* from B1 Unit 21. In both, the subjunctive tells the listener that the situation is not a fact yet."
