+      "content": "The formula has three parts: a verb in the present subjunctive, a relative word (*lo que*, *quien*, *donde*, *como*), and the same verb again. The two verbs always have the same person and tense, because the speaker is talking about one subject: *diga lo que diga*, *digas lo que digas*. The clause can come first, followed by a comma, or last without one: *Voy a terminar este trabajo sea como sea*. A second kind uses *o no* in place of a relative word: *Quieras o no, tienes que ir*."
